  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full 22-song set at The Bluebird in Bloomington, Indiana, on Tuesday, October 15, 2024 [1][3]. This concert is the 431st of 467 archived shows for the band, following a previous recording from October 13, 2024, at the Taft Theatre [3]. The available audio file, taped by SkeletonCounter, runs for 102 minutes and was rated five stars by one listener [1]. The setlist opens with an intro covering Bob Marley and the Wailers' \"Three Little Birds\" before moving into songs like \"Elijah\" and \"Idylls of the King\" [1]. The performance includes a solo segment by John, featuring \"Hebrews 11:40,\" which is a rare track with only 13 archived performances [1][3]. The band then returns as a full group for tracks such as \"Before I Got There\" and \"Transcendental Youth\" [1]. A notable highlight is \"There is Power in a Union,\" a Billy Bragg cover that is the only archived performance of the song [1][3]. The show concludes with an encore containing \"Fresh Tattoo\" and \"No Children\" [1]. A listener review of this specific recording praises the energy and the quality of the audio, noting that the lightweight recording setup captures the trio's dynamic effectively [2]. The tape is described as a treat for fans interested in the band's current configuration [2].",
